Z||000000||Chris Thomas||04-04-2001||02:47 AM||||I am planning on building a Lamborghini Diablo using my 85 SE V6 4spd.  My <BR>next step is to stretch it 10.5 inches to fit the body that I have.  Before <BR>I do the body work, I want to install a V8.  I am currently doing my <BR>research to determine which engine and setup I should use.  I would <BR>appreciate any input from those of you that have gone through a V8 <BR>conversion.  My current thinking is that I want a fuel injected engine that <BR>puts out about 300hp.  I would also like to know if it is a good or a bad <BR>idea to use my existing Fiero 4sp manual tranny. <P>1) Which Engine did you install? <P>2) Fuel Injection or Carb? <P>3) Re-use existing tranny, or swap?  If swap, what did you use? <P>4) I am a little concerned with the Chevy SB requiring the wheel well to be <BR>cut for the water pump.  It looks a little scary.  Did you you choose this <BR>option or other?  If you chose it, how is it working out? <P>5) Where did you get your engine (junk yard, new, rebuilt ...)? <P>6) What other special parts did you use (Archie's conversion kit, special <BR>wiring harness, ...)? <P>7) If you don't mind saying, how much did the swap cost? <P>8) What were the best choices that you made which proved to make the job <BR>easier? <P>9) What would you do differently if you were to do it again? <P>10) Would you do it again? <P>11) Any other advice that you would like to share? <P><BR>Thanks in advance, <P>Chris <BR>85 SE 2m6 <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||rockcrawl||04-04-2001||04:46 PM||||350 TPI, TH3254L longitudinal. <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/longv8.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/longv8.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
